  "assessment": {
    "faithfulness": "Item 2.2 is enforced for this op only: whole emitWhen; imports; resolved-target; filters exactly []; literal absence of endpoint and evidence; file subject kind in policy. Every op-law failure returns POLICY.UNKNOWN_RULE, mapped by bundled admission to HostInvariant/PackDefect::RuleLaw (X12 row 4). Shared registry/ladder/endpoint/plane/filter laws still run; only the relation source-kind membership check is replaced for this op.",
    "bothPasses": "Policy traversal uses depth==1 for root; program traversal carries root=true only for whole emitWhen and false for every boolean operand. Program rules carry no subjectEnumeration. The policy pass checks file kind first, and all three public owners derive or verify exact compilation before this checker, so None in the program pass preserves the joined kind obligation.",
    "unchangedOps": "For every other atom cycle=false, the root bit has no effect and the original source-kind and all other checks stay unchanged. Positive/negative exists controls exercise root and nested positions. Earlier pack test bodies and expectations are byte-identical.",
    "scope": "Only evaluator policy admission and existing cfg(test) pack tests change. atoms.rs/composition.rs, schemas/generated sources, manifests/locks/features, registries/documents, fixtures and design-lock are unchanged. Evaluation retains structural ATOM_OP refusal until I1-b2; release registry has zero rows until I1-c. No crash-matrix lead run set required or run.",
    "coverage": {
      "admission": "Synthetic one-row cfg(test) pack admits the exact I1-P emitWhen for file subjects through real bundled admission, with pack identity, policy/program digests and determinism checked.",
      "violations": "17 schema-admissible policy cases cover boolean nesting, registered wrong relation/rung, lower imports rung, two filters, both explicit endpoints, declared/undeclared evidence, and all three non-file subject kinds. Each asserts exact HostInvariant/RuleLaw UNKNOWN_RULE. n remains a Schema fault.",
      "program": "13 emitWhen violations directly isolate the private program pass; lawful policy/program pairs additionally check file acceptance and symbol policy refusal.",
      "isolatedConjuncts": "Standalone helper checks both Some(file) and None and each conjunct independently, preventing current registry rules from masking omitted relation/evidence checks.",
      "mutations": "Pinned Lead evidence: control passes, all 12 semantic mutants compile and fail the expected tests; M2 and M6 are killed by the standalone test. M11/M12 separately discriminate traversal-root propagation. Base failure before the fourth test and base compile failure with the fourth are accurately distinguished. No mutation rerun."
    }
  },
  "judgmentCalls": {
